] [17592186404160 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404160 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5da5054c-581f-5f31-9886-dad4f588043d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404161 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=0$ and $u=-v.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404161 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404161 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6060e83f-92e8-5d62-986a-7a4aa49b2792" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404162 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the line $u=0$ and on the parabola $u=4{v}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404162 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404162 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1669bc78-1efd-58f9-91e9-a08a66025cf0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404163 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404163 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81279" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404163 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404163 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of $T,$ where $T$ is defined as \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}+3{v}^{2} \\\\ u-2v\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186404163 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "59e9bc67-c967-5c58-a234-d26582651fa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404163 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={u}^{2}+3{v}^{2}$ and $y(u,v)=u-2v.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =6v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 6v \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-2)-6v\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-4u-6v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ -4u-6v & =0 \\\\ 2u+3v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $2u+3v=0$ defines a line in the $uv$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186404164 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404164 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404166 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404164 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404164 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404164 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404164 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404164 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404164 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186404166 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404164 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e87074f0-9d22-553d-826e-78e5774760d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404165 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the line $v=\\frac{2}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404165 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404165 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "27dd60f7-0060-5908-af95-4c108c3b1718" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404166 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the line $2u+3v=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404166 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404166 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ca2acdfc-59b5-5eb0-aa0e-5c6158877fc5" #edb/